“What does it say?” she asked. I handed her the card. I couldn’t speak.
“Did I miss something?” Chris asked. I tried to find the words but my brain was
uncharacteristically empty.
“You can tell Chris all about it later, I don’t want to talk with him in the room right now,”
Orla said with a snap and forceful clarity. Chris frowned.
“What did I do?” Chris asked. Orla pinned emerald green daggers on him.
“Fuck you, Chris.”
Whatever Chris was about to say in response was thankfully cut off when the office door
flung open and Nick came in beaming. I had a terrible ache in my head and Orla slid the
business card into her pocket.
“My team!” he said loudly. “My god. Ellie. Ellie .”
Nick shook his head in awe. Orla smiled despite herself.
“That was fine work. All of you. I think we’re going to get the pull through work. That’s a lot
of revenue you guys. A lot of revenue. He was very impressed with you all.”
Orla raised her thumb to her lips and was biting at her cuticle. I caught her eye and she
dropped her hand to her lap.
“We’re all going out for some drinks. Right now, grab your things,” Nick gushed. He reached
