The pain behind my eyes was blinding. The inconvenience of Friday night, Orla’s infuriating
and inexplicably sudden defiance, and now this… I was furious with myself. Never in my life
had I been this infuriated at anyone and certainly this level of anger was never directed at
myself. She had just made me so angry. The thought of her out on Friday night with Danny’s
greedy eyes on her, his hands on her thigh, buying her drinks…
I grabbed my coat from the rack. I stopped by Orla, who was still sitting.
