in her eyes. The subtle way in which her eyes fluttered around, not looking away, but not
quite looking at the speaker. Her lips were pressed together and the muscles in her face taut. I
wanted to reach out and take her hand.
The elevator doors closed and it was just me, Chris, and Orla for a few moments. I looked at
