“He thought it was funny ,” she said. Voice soft and full of venom. I said nothing. I didn’t
really trust her read on people, but I agreed with her assessment this time. He’d seemed
darkly amused by the situation.
“What are you going to do?” she asked, taking the card out of her pocket and handing it to
me.
“I’m going to the Four Seasons, Presidential Suite alone at six,” I answered. That was
obvious. I needed to know what he wanted. I couldn’t not go. I didn’t think it was likely he’d
try to blackmail me - the man made more in a week than I did in a year, I’d seen the company
