work some of that energy out. It started to hurt and she pressed the heel into my ankle bone. I
felt a burning sensation and something warm and realized she cut me with it.
“Well, you kids take the rest of the day off. I need to head home to the ole wife and kids.”
I slid out of the booth so he could leave. He congratulated us one last time and made for the
door. Once he was out of sight, I picked up her wine glass and walked it back over to the bar.
I gave it to the bartender and told her there was nothing wrong with it. My friend just had a
