“Ah, Mrs. Furst. Sorry to disturb you. A Mr. Caleb Trent here, says he has a meeting with
your husband.”
There was a moment of silence where the man and I held eye contact. My heart was
pounding.
“Yes. Yes, I understand.”
He hung up the phone and I was ready for him to say they had no idea what I was talking
about, but he only smiled and extended a keycard to me.
“Fourth floor, use the elevators to the left, it will bring you right to the suite,” he said. I took
