“Um, scotch, if you have it.”
I tried to keep my voice casual, but there was an undeniable tautness to it. He glanced over
his shoulder with a smirk and then pulled out two glasses.
“If I was going to get you in trouble, I would have done it already,” he said and poured us
two fingers each. He came forward and handed me the glass. I took it with thanks. He
