He carried the scotch over and topped himself off. He made a small offer and I extended my
glass. The word control buzzed around my skull.
“Your boss, Nick Oakes, is an idiot.”
I actually laughed. I couldn’t stop myself. The Austrian looked neither annoyed nor amused
by my laugh.
“He can be,” I agreed. “He’s a nice guy, just… I don’t know, he’s just Nick.”
“He doesn’t take things as seriously as he should,” he said. “There is time for fun and time
