He stared at me. My tongue was hot and thick in my mouth.
“Judging by how pale you look, I would guess you have never had to do this?”
I shook my head.
“I have a friend. But it happened slowly. Over time.”
He nodded in understanding and I felt a flush of kinship. Chris was my best friend. My other
half. A pure, platonic male friendship that knew no bounds. I’d do anything for Chris and
he’d do anything for me. I never once believed I’d meet another person who felt like we did.
I knew others existed, but I never dreamed I’d ever meet them. I let myself imagine,
hopefully, that he might actually be like we were. Not savage monsters who wanted to hurt
and maim - the Bundys and Dahmers. The little smiling girl flashed in my brain, the way the
